{
  "title": "Post-Ziyarat Prayers, Dua & Salawat — Karbala",
  "data": "Two-Unit Prayer at the Head Side\nAt the side of the head, pray 2 units: recite [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) and [Surah al-Rahman](A59) in the first unit, and [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) and [Surah al-Mulk](A71) in the second.",
  "tabs": [
    "Tasbih of Imam Ali & Lady Fatimah\nAfter visiting him, at the head side, repeat the glorification of Amir al-Mu’minin (a.s.) 1,000 times:\nسُبْحَانَ ٱلَّذِي لاَ تَنْفَدُ خَزَائِنُهُ\nSUBHAANAL LAZEE LAA TANFADO KHAZAAA-ENOHU\nGlory be to Him Whose reserves never run out.\nسُبْحَانَ ٱلَّذِي لاَ تَبِيدُ مَعَالِمُهُ\nSUBHAANAL LAZEE LAA TABEEDO MA-A’ALEMOHU\nGlory be to Him Whose signs are never exterminated.\nسُبْحَانَ ٱلَّذِي لاَ يَفْنَىٰ مَا عِنْدَهُ\nSUBHAANAL LAZEE LAA YAFNAA MAA I’NDAHU\nGlory be to Him Whose possessions never expire.\nسُبْحَانَ ٱلَّذِي لاَ يُشْرِكُ احَداً فِي حُكْمِهِ\nSUBHAANAL LAZEE LAA YUSHREKO AHADAN FEE HUKMEHI\nGlory be to Him Who never betakes to Himself a partner in His judgments.\nسُبْحَانَ ٱلَّذِي لاَ ٱضْمِحْلاَلَ لِفَخْرِهِ\nSUBHAANAL LAZEE LAD MEHLAALA LE-FAKHREHI\nGlory be to Him Whose honor never vanishes.\nسُبحَانَ ٱلَّذِي لاَ ٱنْقِطَاعَ لِمُدَّتِهِ\nSUBHAANAL LAZEE LAN QETAA-A’ LE-MUDDATEHI\nGlory be to Him Whose duration (of existence) is never interrupted.\nسُبْحَانَ ٱلَّذِي لاَ إِلٰهَ غَيْرُهُ\nSUBHAANAL LAZEE LAA ELAAHA GHAYROHU\nGlory be to Him save Whom there is no god.\nAt the legs’ side, repeat the glorification of Lady Fatimah (a.s.) 1,000 times:\nسُبْحَانَ ذِي ٱلْجَلاَلِ ٱلْبَاذِخِ ٱلْعَظِيمِ\nSUBHAANA ZIL JALAALIL BAAZEKHIL A’ZEEME\nGlory be to the Lord of lofty, great majesty\nسُبْحَانَ ذِي ٱلْعِزِّ ٱلشَّامِخِ ٱلْمُنِيفِ\nSUBHAANA ZIL I’ZZISH SHAAMEKHIL MONEEFE\nGlory be to the Lord of towering, lofty might\nسُبْحَانَ ذِي ٱلْمُلْكِ ٱلْفَاخِرِ ٱلْقَدِيمِ\nSUBHAANA ZIL MULKIL FAAKHERIL QADEEME\nGlory be to the Lord of eternal, splendid sovereign\nسُبْحَانَ ذِي ٱلْبَهْجَةِ وَٱلْجَمَالِ\nSUBHAANA ZIL BAHJATE WAL JAMAALE\nGlory be to the Lord of splendor and beauty\nسُبْحَانَ مَنْ تَرَدَّىٰ بِٱلنُّورِ وَٱلْوَقَارِ\nSUBHAANA MAN TARADDAA BIN-NOORE WAL WAQAARE\nGlory be to Him Who is clad in light and dignity\nسُبحَانَ مَنْ يَرَىٰ اثَرَ ٱلَّنمْلِ فِي ٱلصَّفَا\nSUBHAANA MAN-Y YARAA ASARAN NAMLE FIS SAFAA\nGlory be to Him Who sees the footprints of the ant on the smooth rock\nوَوَقْعَ ٱلطَّيْرِ فِي ٱلْهَوَاءِ\nWA WAQ-A’T TAYRE FIL HAWAAA-E\nand the alighting of the bird in the air.\nThen pray 2 units, reciting [Surah Ya-Sin](A40) and [Surah al-Rahman](A59).",
    "Salawat on Imam Husayn (a.s.)\nStand behind the tomb at the side of the two shoulders and invoke blessings upon the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) and Imam al-Husayn (a.s.):\nاَللَّهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلَىٰ مُحَمَّدٍ وَآلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLE A’LAA MOHAMMADINW WA AALE MOHAMMADIN\nO Allah, (please) send blessings upon Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad\nوَصَلِّ عَلَىٰ ٱلْحُسَيْنِ ٱلْمَظْلُومِ ٱلشَّهِيدِ\nWA SALLE A’LAL HOSAYNIL MAZLOOMISH SHAHEEDE\nand send blessings upon al-Husayn, the wronged, the martyred,\nقَتِيلِ ٱلْعَبَرَاتِ وَاسِيرِ ٱلْكُرُبَاتِ\nQATEELIL A’BARAATE WA ASEERIL KOROBAATE\nthe victim of shed tears, and the captive of agonies\nصَلاَةً نَامِيَةً زَاكِيَةً مُبَارَكَةً\nSALAATAN NAAMEYATAN ZAAKEYATAM MOBAARAKATAN\nwith ever-increasing, pure, and sacred blessings\nيَصْعَدُ اوَّلُهَا وَلاَ يَنْفَدُ آخِرُهَا\nYAS-A’DO AWWALOHAA WA LAA YANFADO AAKHEROHAA\nthe first of which ascend and the last of which never run out;\nافْضَلَ مَا صَلَّيْتَ عَلَىٰ احَدٍ\nAFZALA MAA SALLAYTA A’LAA AHADIN\nwith the best manner that You have ever conferred upon any\nمِنْ اوْلاَدِ ٱلانْبِيَاءِ وَٱلْمُرْسَلِينَ\nMIN AWLAADIL ANBEYAAA-E WAL MURSALEENA\nof the descendants of the Prophets and Messengers,\nيَا رَبَّ ٱلْعَالِمينَ\nYAA RABBAL A’ALAMEENA\nO Lord of the worlds!\nاَللَّهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلَىٰ ٱلإِمَامِ ٱلشَّهِيدِ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLE A’LAL EMAAMISH SHAHEEDE\nO Allah, send blessings upon the Imam, the martyr,\nٱلْمَقْتُولِ ٱلْمَظْلُومِ ٱلْمَخْذُولِ\nALMAQTOOLIL MAZLOOMIL MAKHZOOLE\nthe slain, the wronged, the forsaken,\nوَٱلسَّيِّدِ ٱلْقَائِدِ وَٱلْعَابِدِ ٱلزَّاهِدِ\nWAS SAYYEDIL QAAA-EDE WAL A’ABEDIZ ZAAHEDE\nthe leading master, the worshipper, the abstemious,\nوَٱلْوَصِيِّ ٱلْخَلِيفَةِ ٱلإِمَامِ ٱلصِّدِّيقِ\nWAL WASIYYIL KHALEEFATIL EMAAMIS SIDDEEQE\nthe successor, the vicegerent, the leader, the veracious,\nٱلطُّهْرِ ٱلطَّاهِرِ ٱلطَّيِّبِ ٱلْمُبَارَكِ\nATTOHRIT TAAHERIT TAYYEBIL MOBAARAKE\nthe pure, the immaculate, the superb, the blessed,\nوَٱلرَّضِيِّ ٱلْمَرْضِيِّ وَٱلتَّقِيِّ ٱلْهَادِي ٱلْمَهْدِيِّ\nWAR RAZIYYIL MARZIYYE WAT TAQIYYIL HAADIL MAHDIYYE\nthe amiable, the pleased, the pious, the guide, the well-guided,\nٱلزَّاهِدِ ٱلذَّائِدِ ٱلْمُجَاهِدِ ٱلْعَالِمِ\nAZZAAHEDIZ ZAAA-EDIL MOJAAHEDIL A’ALEME\nthe abstemious, the defender (of Islam), the striver, the knowledgeable,\nإِمَامِ ٱلْهُدَىٰ سِبْطِ ٱلرَّسُولِ وَقُرَّةِ عَيْنِ ٱلْبَتُولِ\nEMAAMIL HODAA SIBTIR RASOOLE WA QURRATE A’YNIL BATOOLE\nthe leader of true guidance, the grandson of the Messenger, and the delight of the eye of the Chaste Lady.\nاَللَّهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلَىٰ سَيِّدِي وَمَوْلاَيَ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLE A’LAA SAYYEDEE WA MAWLAAYA\nO Allah, send blessings upon my master and chief\nكَمَا عَمِلَ بِطَاعَتِكَ\nKAMAA A’MELA BE-TAA-A’TEKA\nfor he acted obediently to You,\nوَنَهَىٰ عَنْ مَعْصِيَتِكَ\nWA NAHAA A’M MA’SEYATEKA\nwarned against disobeying You,\nوَبَالَغَ فِي رِضْوَانِكَ\nWA BAALAGHA FEE RIZWAANEKA\nmade all efforts to attain Your pleasure,\nوَاقْبَلَ عَلَىٰ إِيمَانِكَ\nWA AQBALA A’LAA EEMAANEKA\nwarmly received belief in You,\nغَيْرَ قَابِل فِيكَ عُذْراً\nGHAYRA QAABELIN FEEKA U’ZRAN\nrejected all excuses against You,\nسِرّاً وَعَلاَنِيَةً يَدْعُو ٱلْعِبَادِ إِلَيْكَ\nSIRRANW WA A’LAANEYATAN-Y YAD-U’L E’BAADE ELAYKA\ncalled the servants to You secretly and openly,\nوَيَدُلُّهُمْ عَلَيْكَ\nWA YADULLOHUM A’LAYKA\nshowed them the way to You,\nوَقَامَ بَيْنَ يَدَيْكَ\nWA QAAMA BAYNA YADAYKA\nundertook in obedience to You the mission\nيَهْدِمُ ٱلْجَوْرَ بِٱلصَّوَابِ\nYAHDEMUL JAWRA BIS-SAWAABE\nof demolishing inequity with rectitude\nوَيُحْيِي ٱلسُّنَّةَ بِٱلْكِتَابِ\nWA YOHYIS SUNNATA BIL-KETAABE\nand refreshing the traditions in the (light of the) Book.\nفَعَاشَ فِي رِضْوَانِكَ مَكْدُوداً\nFA-A’ASHA FEE RIZWAANEKA MAKDOODAN\nSo, he lived in fatigue for the sake of Your pleasure\nوَمَضَىٰ عَلَىٰ طَاعَتِكَ وَفِي اوْلِيَائِكَ مَكْدُوحاً\nWA MAZAA A’LAA TAA-A’TEKA WA FEE AWLEYAAA-EKA MAKDOOHAN\nand passed away in obedience to You, working hard for the sake of Your Intimate Servants.\nوَقَضَىٰ إِلَيْكَ مَفْقُوداً\nWA QAZAA ELAYKA MAFQOODAN\nHe thus joined You missed (by the believers).\nلَمْ يَعْصِكَ فِي لَيْلٍ وَلاَ نَهَارٍ\nLAM YA’SEKA FEE LAYLINW WA LAA NAHAARIN\nHe never disobeyed You; neither at night nor in day;\nبَلْ جَاهَدَ فِيكَ ٱلْمُنَافِقِينَ وَٱلْكُفَّارَ\nBAL JAAHADA FEEKAL MONAAFEQEENA WAL KUFFAARA\nrather, he, for Your sake, strove against the hypocrites and the unbelievers.\nاَللَّهُمَّ فَٱجْزِهِ خَيْرَ جَزَاءِ ٱلصَّادِقِينَ ٱلابْرَارِ\nALLAAHUMMA FAJZEHI KHAYRA JAZAAA-IS SAADEQEENAL ABRAARE\nSo, O Allah, (please) award him with the best reward of the veracious and the righteous\nوَضَاعِفْ عَلَيْهِمُ ٱلْعَذَابَ وَلِقَاتِلِيهِ ٱلْعِقَابَ\nWA ZAA-I’F A’LAYHEMUL A’ZAABA WA LE-QAATELEEHIL E’QAABA\nand multiply the chastisement and the punishment for those who slew him.\nفَقَدْ قَاتَلَ كَرِيماً وَقُتِلَ مَظْلُوماً وَمَضَىٰ مَرْحُوماً\nFAQAD QAATALA KAREEMANW WA QOTELA MAZLOOMANW WA MAZAA MARHOOMAN\nVerily, he fought with nobility, was slain wrongly, and passed away enjoying mercy.\nيَقُولُ انَا ٱبْنُ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nYAQOOLO ANABNO RASOOLIL LAAHE MOHAMMADIN\nHe said to them, “I am the son of Allah’s Messenger Muhammad\nوَٱبْنُ مَنْ زَكَّىٰ وَعَبَدَ\nWABNO MAN ZAKKAA WA A’BADA\nand the son of him who gave alms and served Allah.\nفَقَتَلُوهُ بِٱلْعَمْدِ ٱلْمُعْتَمَدِ\nFAQATALOOHO BIL-A’MDIL MO’TAMADE\nYet, they slew him clearly intentionally.\nقَتَلُوهُ عَلَىٰ ٱلإِيمَانِ\nQATALOOHO A’LAL EEMAANE\nThey slew him because of his faith;\nوَاطَاعُوٱ فِي قَتْلِهِ ٱلشَّيْطَانَ\nWA ATAA-O’ FEE QATLEHISH SHAYTAANA\ntherefore, they obeyed Satan\nوَلَمْ يُرَاقِبُوٱ فِيهِ ٱلرَّحْمٰنَ\nWA LAM YORAAQEBO FEEHIR RAHMAANA\nand never cared for the All-beneficent Lord.\nاَللَّهُمَّ فَصَلِّ عَلَىٰ سَيِّدِي وَمَوْلاَيَ\nALLAAHUMMA FASALLE A’LAA SAYYEDEE WA MAWLAAYA\nSo, O Allah, (please) send upon my master and chief\nصَلاَةً تَرْفَعُ بِهَا ذِكْرَه\nSALAATAN TARFA-O’ BEHAA ZIKRAHU\nsuch blessings by which You raise his eminence,\nوَتُظْهِرُ بِهَا امْرَهُ\nWA TUZHERO BEHAA AMRAHU\nmake prevalent his issue,\nوَتُعَجِّلُ بِهَا نَصْرَهُ\nWA TO-A’JJELO BEHAA NASRAHU\nand hasten his victory.\nوَٱخْصُصْهُ بِافْضَلِ قِسَمِ ٱلْفَضَائِلِ يَوْمَ ٱلْقِيَامَةِ\nWAKH SUS-HO BE-AFZALE QESAMIL FAZAAA-ELE YAWMAL QEYAAMATE\nAnd (please) endue him on the Resurrection day with the best of Your favors,\nوَزِدْهُ شَرَفاً فِي اعَلىٰ عِلِّيِّينَ\nWA ZID-HO SHARAFAN FEE A-A’LAA I’LLIYYEENA\nincrease his honor to the highest degree of the Supreme Rank,\nوَبَلِّغْهُ اعَلَىٰ شَرَفِ ٱلْمُكَرَّمِينَ\nWA BALLIGH-HO A-A’LAA SHARAFIL MOKARRAMEENA\ntake him higher to the highest rank of the honored ones,\nوَٱرْفَعْهُ مِنْ شَرَفِ رَحْمَتِكَ\nWAR FA’HO MIN SHARAFE RAHMATEKA\nraise him in the honor of Your mercy\nفِي شَرَفِ ٱلْمُقَرَّبِينَ\nFEE SHARAFIL MOQARRABEENA\nto the honor of the most favorable ones\nفِي ٱلرَّفيعِ ٱلاعَلىٰ\nFIR RAFEE-I’L A-A’LAA\nin the Highest Level,\nوَبَلِّغْهُ ٱلْوَسِيلَةَ وَٱلْمَنْزِلَةَ ٱلْجَلِيلَةَ\nWA BALLIGH-HUL WASEELATA WAL MANZELATAL JALEELATA\ngrant him the right of mediation, the loftiest position,\nوَٱلْفَضْلَ وَٱلْفَضِيلَةَ\nWAL FAZLA WAL FAZEELATA\nthe superiority, the excellence,\nوَٱلْكِرَامَةَ ٱلْجَزِيلَةَ\nWAL KERAAMATAL JAZEELATA\nand the abundant privilege.\nاَللَّهُمَّ فَٱجْزِهِ عَنَّا افْضَلَ مَا جَازَيْتَ إِمَاماً عَنْ رَعِيَّتِهِ\nALLAAHUMMA FAJZEHI A’NNAA AFZALA MAA JAAZAYTA EMAAMAN A’R RA-I’YYATEHI\nO Allah, (please) award him on behalf of us with the most excellent reward that You have ever given to a leader on behalf of his subjects\nوَصَلِّ عَلَىٰ سَيِّدِي وَمَوْلاَيَ كُلَّمَا ذُكِرَ\nWA SALLE A’LAA SAYYEDEE WA MAWLAAYA KULLAMAA ZOKERA\nand bless my master and chief whenever he is mentioned\nوَكُلَّمَا لَمْ يُذْكَرْ\nWA KULLAMAA LAM YUZKAR\nand whenever he is not.\nيَا سَيِّدِي وَمَوْلاَيَ\nYAA SAYYEDEE WA MAWLAAYA\nO my master and chief,\nادْخِلْنِي فِي حِزْبِكَ وَزُمْرَتِكَ\nADKHILNEE FEE HIZBEKA WA ZUMRATEKA\ninclude me with your party and group\nوَٱسْتَوْهِبْنِي مِنْ رَبِّكَ وَرَبِّي\nWAS TAWHIBNEE MIR RABBEKA WA RABBEE\nand ask my and your Lord to release me as grant from Him to you,\nفَإِنَّ لَكَ عِنْدَ ٱللَّهِ جَاهاً وَقَدْراً\nFA-INNA LAKA I’NDAL LAAHE JAAHANW WA QADRAN\nfor you verily enjoy a special esteem and value with Allah\nوَمَنْزِلَةً رَفيعَةً\nWA MANZELATAR RAFEE-A’TAN\nas well as a lofty standing:\nإِنْ سَالْتَ اعْطِيتَ\nIN SA-ALTA O’TEETA\nif you ask, He gives you\nوَإِنْ شَفَعْتَ شُفِّعْتَ\nWA IN SHAFA’TA SHUFFE’TA\nand if you intercede, He admits your intercession.\nاللَّهَ اللَّهَ فِي عَبْدِكَ وَمَوْلاَكَ\nALLAAHAL LAAHA FEE A’BDEKA WA MAWLAAKA\nBy Allah I ask you to regard me, your slave and servant.\nلاََ تُخَلِّنِي عِنْدَ ٱلشَّدَائِدِ وَٱلاهْوَالِ\nLAA TOKHALLENEE I’NDASH SHADAAA-EDE WAL AHWAALE\nDo not desert me at the time of ordeals and horrors\nلِسُوءِ عَمَلِي وَقَبِيحِ فِعْلِي وَعَظِيمِ جُرْمِي\nLE-SOO-E A’MALEE WA QABEEHE FE’LEE WA A’ZEEME JURMEE\nbecause of my evildoing, misconduct, and enormous offenses.\nفَإِنَّكَ امَلِي وَرَجَائِي\nFA-INNAKA AMALEE WA RAJAAA-EE\nYou are verily my hope and my wish,\nوَثِقَتِي وَمُعْتَمَدِي\nWA SEQATEE WA MO’TAMADEE\nI have confidence in you, I rely upon you,\nوَوَسِيلَتِي إِلَىٰ ٱللَّهِ رَبِّي وَرَبِّكَ\nWA WASEELATEE ELAL LAAHE RABBEE WA RABBEKA\nand you are my means to Allah, my and your Lord.\nلَمْ يَتَوَسَّلِ ٱلْمُتَوَسِّلُونَ إِلَىٰ ٱللَّهِ\nLAM YATAWASSALIL MOTAWASSELOONA ELAL LAAHE\nNo means that has been made to Allah\nبِوَسِيلَة هِيَ اعْظَمُ حَقّاً\nBE-WASEELATIN HEYA A-A’ZAMO HAQQAN\nis greater in status,\nوَلاَ اوْجَبُ حُرْمَةً\nWA LAA AWJABO HURMATAN\nmore incumbent in sanctity,\nوَلاَ اجَّلُ قَدْراً\nWA LAA AJALLO QADRAN\nor loftier in eminence\nعِنْدَهُ مِنْكُمْ اهْلَ ٱلْبَيْتِ\nI’NDAHU MINKUM AHLAL BAYTE\nthan yours, the Ahl al-Bayt, in the sight of Allah.\nلاََ خَلَّفَنِيَ ٱللَّهُ عَنْكُمْ بِذُنُوبِي\nLAA KHALLAFANEYAL LAAHO A’NKUM BE-ZONOOBEE\nMay Allah never cause me to lag behind you because of my sins\nوَجَمَعَنِي وَإِيَّاكُمْ فِي جَنَّةِ عَدْنٍ\nWA JAMA-A’NEE WA IYYAAKUM FEE JANNATE A’DNIN\nand may He join me with you in the perpetual abode of Paradise\nٱلَّتِي اعَدَّهَا لَكُمْ وَلاِوْلِيَائِكُمْ\nALLATEE A-A’DDAHAA LAKUM WA LE-AWLEYAAA-EKUM\nthat He has prepared for you and your loyalists.\nإِنَّهُ خَيْرُ ٱلْغَافِرِينَ وَارْحَمَ ٱلرَّاحِمِينَ\nINNAHU KHAYRUL GHAAFEREENA WA ARHAMUR RAAHEMEENA\nVerily, He is the best of all those who may forgive and the most merciful of all those who show mercy.\nاَللَّهُمَّ ابْلِغْ سَيِّدِي وَمَوْلاَيَ\nALLAAHUMMA ABLIGH SAYYEDEE WA MAWLAAYA\nO Allah, (please) convey to my master and chief\nتَحِيَّةً كَثِيرَةً وَسَلاَماً\nTAHIYYATAN KASEERATANW WA SALAAMAN\nabundant greetings and salutations\nوَٱرْدُدْ عَلَيْنَا مِنْهُ ٱلسَّلاَمَ\nWAR DUD A’LAYNAA MINHUS SALAAMA\nand convey to us his response to our greetings.\nإِنَّكَ جَوَادٌ كَرِيمٌ\nINNAKA JAWAADUN KAREEMUN\nYou are verily All-magnanimous and All-generous.\nوَصَلِّ عَلَيْهِ كُلَّمَا ذُكِرَ ٱلسَّلاَمُ\nWA SALLE A’LAYHE KULLAMAA ZOKERAS SALAAMO\nAnd bless him whenever blessing is mentioned\nوَكُلَّمَا لَمْ يُذْكَرْ يَا رَبَّ ٱلْعَالَمِينَ\nWA KULLAMAA LAM YUZKAR YAA RABBAL A’ALAMEENA\nand whenever it is not mentioned, O Lord of the worlds!",
    "Dua Allahumma Qad Tara Makani\nPray earnestly to Almighty Allah at the shrine: turn to Him, repent before Him and present your needs. The supplications of al-Sahifah al-Sajjadiyyah are the most preferable.\nRaise your hands towards the sky and recite:\nاَللَّهُمَّ قَدْ تَرَىٰ مَكَانِي\nALLAAHUMMA QAD TARAA MAKAANEE\nO Allah, You do see my place,\nوَتَسْمَعُ كَلاَمِي\nWA TASMA-O’ KALAAMEE\nhear my words,\nوَتَرَىٰ مَقَامِي وَتَضَرُّعِي\nWA TARAA MAQAAMEE WA TAZARRO-E’E\nand see my situation, imploration,\nوَمَلاَذِي بِقَبْرِ حُجَّتِكَ وَٱبْنِ نَبِيِّكَ\nWA MALAAZEE BE-QABRE HUJJATEKA WABNE NABIYYEKA\nand seeking shelter with the tomb of Your Argument and Your Prophet’s son.\nوَقَدْ عَلِمْتَ يَا سَيِّدِي حَوَائِجِي\nWA QAD A’LIMTA YAA SAYYEDEE HAWAAA-EJEE\nYou, O my Master, have already known my needs\nوَلاَ يَخْفَىٰ عَلَيْكَ حَالِي\nWA LAA YAKHFAA A’LAYKA HAALEE\nand none of my manners can be hidden from You.\nوَقَدْ تَوَجَّهْتُ إِلَيْكَ بِٱبْنِ رَسُولِكَ\nWA QAD TAWAJJAHTO ELAYKA BIBNE RASOOLEKA\nI am now turning my face towards You in the name of Your Prophet’s son,\nوَحُجَّتِكَ وَامِينِكَ\nWA HUJJATEKA WA AMEENEKA\nYour Argument, and Your trustee.\nوَقَدْ اتَيْتُكَ مُتَقَرِّباً بِهِ إِلَيْكَ وَإِلىٰ رَسُولِكَ\nWA QAD ATAYTOKA MOTAQARREBAN BEHI ELAYKA WA ELAA RASOOLEKA\nI have come to You seeking nearness to You in his name and in the name of Your Messenger.\nفَٱجْعَلْنِي بِهِ عِنْدَكَ وَجِيهاً\nFAJ-A’LNEE BEHI I’NDAKA WAJEEHAN\nSo, (please), in his name, make me worthy of regard with You\nفِي ٱلدُّنْيَا وَالآخِرَةِ وَمِنَ ٱلْمُقَرَّبِينَ\nFID DUNYAA WAL AAKHERATE WA MENAL MOQARRABEENA\nin this world and in the Hereafter and (make me) of those drawn near to You.\nوَاعْطِنِي بِزِيَارَتِي امَلِي\nWA A-A’TENEE BE-ZEYAARATEE AMALEE\nAnd grant me, due to this visit of mine, what I hope,\nوَهَبْ لِي مُنَايَ\nWA HAB LEE MONAAYA\nendue me with my wish,\nوَتَفَضَّلْ عَلَيَّ بِشَهْوَتِي وَرَغْبَتِي\nWA TAFAZZAL A’LAYYA BE-SHAHWATEE WA RAGHBATEE\nfavor me with my desire and aspiration,\nوَٱقْضِ لِي حَوَائِجِي\nWAQ ZE LEE HAWAAA-EJEE\nsettle for me my needs,\nوَلاَ تَرُدَّنِي خَائِباً\nWA LAA TARUDDANEE KHAAA-EBAN\ndo not reject me with disappointment,\nوَلاَ تَقْطَعْ رَجَائِي\nWA LAA TAQTA’ RAJAAA-EE\ndo not cut off my hope (in You),\nوَلاَ تُخَيِّبْ دُعَائِي\nWA LAA TOKHAYYIB DO-A’A-EE\ndo not let down my prayer,\nوَعَرِّفْنِي ٱلإِجَابَةِ فِي جَمِيعِ مَا دَعَوْتُكَ\nWA A’RRIFNIL EJAABATE FEE JAMEE-E’ MAA DA-A’WTOKA\nshow me proofs of Your response to all that which I prayed You for,\nمِنْ امْرِ ٱلدِّينِ وَٱلدُّنْيَا وَٱلآخِرَةِ\nMIN AMRID DEENE WAD DUNYAA WAL AAKHERATE\nincluding the affairs of my religion, worldly life, and the Hereafter,\nوَٱجْعَلْنِي مِنْ عِبَادِكَ\nWAJ A’LNEE MIN E’BAADEKA\ninclude me with Your servants\nٱلَّذِينَ صَرَفْتَ عَنْهُمُ ٱلْبَلاَيَا وَٱلامْرَاضَ\nALLAZEENA SARAFTA A’NHOMUL BALAAYAA WAL AMRAAZA\nfrom whom You have warded off misfortunes, diseases,\nوَٱلْفِتَنَ وَٱلاعْرَاضَ\nWAL FETANA WAL A-A’RAAZA\nseditious matters, and calamities;\nمِنَ ٱلذِّينَ تُحْيِيهِمْ فِي عَافِيَةٍٍ\nMENAL LAZEENA TOHYEEHIM FEE A’AFEYATIN\nthose whom You make live in wellbeing,\nوَتُميتُهُمْ فِي عَافِيَةٍ\nWA TOMEETOHUM FEE A’AFEYATIN\ncause to die in wellbeing,\nوَتُدْخِلُهُمُ ٱلْجَنَّةَ فِي عَافِيَةٍ\nWA TUDKHELOHOMUL JANNATA FEE A’AFEYATIN\nallow to enter Paradise in wellbeing,\nوَتُجِيرُهُمْ مِنَ ٱلنَّارِ فِي عَافِيَةٍ\nWA TOJEEROHUM MENAN NAARE FEE A’AFEYATIN\nand save from Hellfire in wellbeing;\nوَوَفِّقْ لِي بِمَنٍّ مِنْكَ\nWA WAFFIQ LEE BEMANNIM MINKA\nand, out of Your favor, lead me\nصَلاَحَ مَا اؤَمِلَّ فِي نَفْسِي\nSALAAHA MAA O-AMMELO FEE NAFSEE\nto the achievement of what I hope for regarding myself,\nوَاهْلِي وَوُلْدِي وَإِخْوَانِي وَمَالِي\nWA AHLEE WA WULDEE WA IKHWAANEE WA MAALEE\nmy wife, my sons, my brethren-in-faith, my properties,\nوَجَمِيعِ مَا انْعَمْتَ بِهِ عَلَيَّ\nWA JAMEE-E’ MAA AN-A’MTA BEHI A’LAYYA\nand whatever bliss You have endowed me;\nيَا ارْحَمَ ٱلرَّاحِمينَ\nYAA ARHAMAR RAAHEMEENA\nO most merciful of all those who show mercy!",
    "Dua of the Oppressed\nIf you have been wronged by an oppressor, pray with this supplication in the holy shrine of Imam al-Husayn (a.s.):\nاَللَّهُمَّ إِنِّي اعْتَزُّ بِدِينِكَ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE A-A’TAZZO BE-DEENEKA\nO Allah, I obtain my dignity from following Your religion\nوَاكْرُمُ بِهِدَايَتِكَ\nWA AKROMO BE-HEDAAYATEKA\nand I am honored because of You have guided me,\nوَ… يُذِلُّنِي بِشَرِّهِ\nWA YOZILLONEE BE-SHARREHI\nbut [so-and-so] is humiliating me by his evil,\nوَيُهِينُنِي بِاذِيَّتِهِ\nWA YOHEENONEE BE-AZIYYATEHI\ninsulting me by harming me,\nوَيُعِيبُنِي بِوَلاَءِ اوْلِيَائِكَ\nWA YO-E’EBONEE BE-WALAAA-E AWLEYAAA-EKA\nimputing dishonor to me because I am loyal to Your Representatives,\nوَيَبْهَتُنِي بِدَعْوَاهُ\nWA YABHATONEE BE-DA’WAAHO\nand charging me with false claims.\nوَقَدْ جِئْتُ إِلَىٰ مَوْضِعِ ٱلدُّعَاءِ\nWA QAD JEATO ELAA MAWZE-I’D DO-A’A-E\nI have come to the center of supplication\nوَضَمَانِكَ ٱلإِجَابَةَ\nWA ZAMAANEKAL EJAABATA\nand the guarantee of response.\nاَللَّهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلَىٰ مُحَمَّدٍ وَآلِ مُحَمَّدٍٍ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLE A’LAA MOHAMMADINW WA AALE MOHAMMADIN\nO Allah, (please) send blessings upon Muhammad and his Household\nوَاعِدْنِي عَلَيْهِ ٱلسَّاعَةَ ٱلسَّاعَةَ\nWA A-I’DNEE A’LAYHIS SAA-A’TAS SAA-A’TA\nand support me against him at this very hour! At this very hour!\nThen throw yourself on the grave and say:\nمَوْلاَيَ إِمَامِي\nMAWLAAYA EMAAMEE\nO my master and leader,\nمَظْلُومٌ ٱسْتَعْدَىٰ عَلَىٰ ظَالِمِهِ\nMAZLOOMONIS TA’DAA A’LAA ZAALEMEHI\n(I have been) oppressed and (I am) seeking your support against him who has oppressed me.\nٱلنَّصْرَ ٱلنَّصْرَ\nANNASRAN NASRA\nGrant me support! Grant me support!\nThe last statement may be repeated as many times as one breath may take.",
    "Short Dua at the Head Side\nAt the side of Imam al-Husayn’s head, for the granting of requests, recite:\nيَا ابَا عَبْدِ ٱللَّهِ\nYAA ABAA A’BDIL LAAHE\nO Abu-`Abdullah,\nاشْهَدُ انَّكَ تَشْهَدُ مَقَامِي\nASH-HADO ANNAKA TASH-HADO MAQAAMEE\nI bear witness that you can now see my situation\nوَتَسْمَعُ كَلاَمِي\nWA TASMA-O’ KALAAMEE\nand hear my words\nوَانَّكَ حَيٌّ عِنْدَ رَبِّكَ تُرْزَقُ\nWA ANNAKA HAYYUN I’NDA RABBEKA TURZAQO\nand that you are alive with Your Lord and you are receiving sustenance from Him.\nفَٱسْالْ رَبَّكَ وَرَبِّي فِي قَضَاءِ حَوَائِجِي\nFAS-AL RABBAKA WA RABBEE FEE QAZAAA-E HAWAAA-EJEE\nSo (please) ask your and my Lord to grant me my requests.",
    "Longer Dua at the Head Side\nPray 2 units: after [Surah al-Fatihah](A5), recite [Surah al-Anbiya](A25) in the first unit and [Surah al-Hashr](A63) in the second. In the qunoot, recite:\nلاإِلهَ إِلاَّ اللهُ الْحَليمُ الْكَريمُ ،\nLAA ELAAHA ILLAL LAAHUL HALEEMUL KAREEMO\nThere is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Generous,\nلاإِلهَ إِلاَّاللهُ الْعَلِىُّ الْعَظيمُ ،\nLAA ELAAHA ILLAL LAAHUL A’LIYYUL A’ZEEMO\nThere is no god but Allah, the Most High, the Great,\nلاإِلهَ إِلاَّاللهُ رَبُّ السَّماواتِ السَّبْعِ ،\nLAA ELAAHA ILLAL LAAHO RABBUS SAMAAWAATIS SAB-E’\nThere is no god but Allah, the Lord of the seven heavens,\nوالاَْرَضينَ السَّبْعِ ،\nWAL ARAZEENAS SAB-E’\nAnd of the seven earths,\nوَما فيهِنَّ ،\nWA MAA FEEHINNA\nAnd whatever is in them,\nوما بَيْنَهُنَّ ،\nWA MAA BAYNAHUNNA\nAnd whatever is between them,\nخِلافاً لاَِعْدآئِهِ ،\nKHELAAFAL LE-A-A’DAAA-EHI\nOpposing His enemies,\nوَتَكْذيباً لِمَنْ عَدَلَ بِهِ ،\nWA TAKZEEBAL LEMAN A’DALA BEHI\nAnd denying those who equate anything with Him,\nوَإِقْراراً لِرُبُوبِيَّتِهِ ،\nWA IQRAARAL LE-ROBOOBIYYATEHI\nAnd acknowledging His lordship,\nوَخُضُوعاً لِعِزَّتِهِ ،\nWA KHOZOO-A’L LE-I’ZZATEHI\nAnd submitting to His might,\nالاَْوَّلُ بِغَيْرِ أَوَّل ،\nAL-AWWALO BE-GHAYRE AWWALIN\nThe First without a beginning,\nوالاْخِرُ إِلى غَيْرِ اخِر ،\nWAL AAKHERO ELAA GHAYRE AAKHERIN\nAnd the Last without an end,\nالظّاهِرُ عَلى كُلِّ شَىْء بِقُدْرَتِهِ ،\nAZZAAHERO A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IM BE-QUDRATEHI\nThe Manifest above everything by His power,\nالْباطِنُ دُونَ كُلِّ شَىْء بِعِلْمِهِ وَلُطْفِهِ ،\nALBAATENO DOONA KULLE SHAY-IM BE-I’LMEHI WA LUTFEHI\nThe Hidden beyond everything by His knowledge and subtlety,\nلا تَقِفُ الْعُقُولُ عَلى كُنْهِ عَظَمَتِهِ ،\nLAA TAQEFUL O’QOOLO A’LAA KUNHE A’ZAMATEHI\nMinds cannot comprehend the essence of His greatness,\nولاتُدْرِكُ الاَْوْهامُ حَقيقَةَ ماهِيَّتِهِ ،\nWA LAA TUDREKUL AWHAAMO HAQEEQATA MAAHIYYATEHI\nAnd imaginations cannot perceive the reality of His nature,\nولاتَتَصَوَّرُ الاَْنْفُسُ مَعانِىَ كَيْفِيَّتِهِ ،\nWA LAA TATASAWWARUL ANFOSO MA-A’ANEYA KAYFIYYATEHI\nAnd souls cannot conceive the meanings of His how-ness,\nمُطَّلِعاً عَلَى الضَّمآئِرِ ،\nMUTTALE-A’N A’LAZ ZAMAAA-ERE\nAware of the consciences,\nعارِفاً بِالسَّرآئِرِ ،\nA’AREFAM BIS-SARAAA-ERE\nKnowing the secrets,\nيَعْلَمُ خآئِنَةَ الاَْعْيُنِ ،\nYA’LAMO KHAAA-ENATAL A-A’YONE\nHe knows the betrayal of the eyes,\nوَما تُخْفِى الصُّدُورُ ،\nWA MAA TUKHFIS SODOORO\nAnd what the breasts conceal,\nأَللّٰهُمَّ إِنّي اُشْهِدُك َ عَلى تَصْديقي رَسُولَك َ ،\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE USH-HEDOKA A’LAA TASDEEQEE RASOOLAKA\nO Allah, I bear witness to my belief in Your Messenger,\nصَلَّى اللهُ عَلَيْهِ وَالِهِ ،\nSALLAL LAAHO A’LAYHE WA AALEHI\nPeace be upon him and his family,\nوَإيماني بِهِ ،\nWA EEMAANEE BEHI\nAnd my faith in him,\nAfter completing the Salat , recite tasbeeh of Hazrat Sayyada s.a. and then go in prostration and recite the following forty times:"
  ],
  "merits": "Two-unit prayer: On the word of Sayyid Ibn Tawus, one who offers this prayer will be granted the reward of having performed an admitted and acceptable ritual pilgrimage (hajj) with the Holy Prophet (s) for twenty times.\n\nTasbih of Imam Ali and Lady Fatimah: Abu-Sa`id al-Mada'ini is reported to have said that he, once, came to Imam al-Sadiq ('a) and asked, “May I go for visiting the tomb of al-Husayn?” The Imam ('a) answered, “Yes, you may. Go for visiting the tomb of al-Husayn the son of Allah’s Messenger, the most immaculate of all the immaculate ones, the most infallible of all the infallible ones, and the most munificent of all those who act munificently. After you visit him, you may repeat the glorification words of the Commander of the Faithful (Amir al-Mu'minin) one thousand times while you are at the head’s side and repeat the glorification words of the Luminous Lady (i.e. al-Zahra') one thousand time while you are at the legs’ side. You may then offer a two-unit prayer reciting [Surah Yasin](A40) (No. 36) and [Surah al-Rahman](A59) (No. 55) in that prayer. If you do so, you will earn a great reward.”\n\nSalawat on Imam Husayn: Among the rites to be done in the holy shrine of Imam al-Husayn ('a) is to invoke Almighty Allah’s blessings upon him. It is thus reported to stand behind the tomb at the side of the two shoulders and to invoke Almighty Allah’s blessings upon the Holy Prophet (s) and Imam al-Husayn ('a).\n\nIn his book of Misbah al-Za'ir, Sayyid Ibn Tawus has reported this form of invocation of blessings upon Imam al-Husayn ('a) within some forms of ziyarah.\n\nDua Allahumma Qad Tara Makani: Granting of requests under the supreme dome of his shrine is one of the distinctive returns that Almighty Allah has exclusively given to Imam al-Husayn ('a) as one compensation for his martyrdom. Seizing this opportunity, a pilgrim is advised not to show any shortcoming in entreating Almighty Allah, turning to Him, repenting before Him, and providing one’s needs to Him.\n\nDua of the Oppressed: Among the recommended acts in the shrine of Imam al-Husayn ('a) is to say the supplicatory prayer of the oppressed against the oppressor . In other words, one who has been exposed to wronging by an oppressor is advised to pray Almighty Allah with this supplicatory prayer in the holy shrine of Imam al-Husayn ('a). This supplicatory prayer, which has been recorded by Shaykh al-Tusi in his book of Misbah al-Mutahajjid to be one of the recommended acts on Fridays.\n\nShort dua: It has been reported by Ibn Fahad in his book of `Uddat al-Da`i.\n\nHe who says this supplication will have his requested granted by Almighty Allah, God willing.\n\nLonger dua: Source: Biharul Anwar, vol. 98, page 324."
